@startuml Tseten Database Architecture
!define RECTANGLE_WIDTH 280
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam wrapWidth 250
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

title Tseten Dual Database Strategy - Data Storage Architecture
scale 0.9

skinparam database {
    BackgroundColor #E8F5E9
    BorderColor #2E7D32
}

skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1976D2
}

package "Tseten.Infrastructure" as infra {
    component [TsetenContext] as couchContext
    component [VectorDbContext] as vectorContext
    component [EmbeddingService] as embeddingService
}

database "Couchbase Lite" as couchbase
database "SQL Server" as sqlserver

' Relationships
couchContext --> couchbase : reads/writes documents
vectorContext --> sqlserver : EF Core mapping
embeddingService --> vectorContext : uses
embeddingService --> sqlserver : query vectors

note right of couchContext
  **Couchbase Lite Context**
  - Database : Database
  - GetCollection<T>()
  - SaveDocument<T>()
  - GetDocument<T>(id)
  - Query<T>(predicate)
  - DeleteDocument(id)
  
  Implements ITsetenContext
  Document-based operations
end note

note right of vectorContext
  **EF Core DbContext**
  - Embeddings : DbSet<Embedding>
  - OnModelCreating()
  - SaveChangesAsync()
  
  SQL Server vector storage
  Entity Framework Core
end note

note right of embeddingService
  **Vector Embedding Service**
  - GenerateEmbedding(text)
  - SearchBySimilarity(query, threshold)
  - CosineSimilarity(v1, v2)
  
  384-dimensional vectors
  Semantic search operations
end note

note right of couchbase
  **Embedded NoSQL Database**
  No separate server process needed.
  Database files stored locally with app.
  
  **Collections:**
  - software-requirements
  - tags
  - users
  - profiles
  
  **Format:** JSON documents
  Schema-less flexibility
  Offline-first capable
end note

note right of sqlserver
  **Vector Database**
  Requires SQL Server or SQL Express.
  
  **Table: Embeddings**
  - Id (int, PK, Identity)
  - SoftwareRequirementId (string)
  - Embedding (float[], 384 dims)
  - LastUpdated (DateTime)
  
  Indexed for cosine similarity
  
  **Why Dual Database?**
  1. Couchbase: Fast document retrieval
  2. SQL Server: Optimized vector queries
end note

@enduml
